# The build context is the **repository root** (context: .. in compose).
# Without these exclusions the builder walks the runtime data directory, which holds private
# files written by uid 10001 inside a container (`.claude/sessions` is 0700), and the build
# dies on the spot:
#
#   error from sender: open data/workspaces/<uid>/.agent-home/.claude/sessions: permission denied
#
# Note this only bites **after the first deployment**: on a clean clone data/ does not exist
# yet, so the first build sails through.
# And even with permissions opened up it has no business in the context — that directory holds
# every user's complete conversations and traces.
data/
data.backup-*/
log/
trace-proxy/traces*/

# The image runs its own npm ci; the host's copy may not even be for the same platform (native modules)
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/

# Credentials and local build output — none of it belongs in an image
.env
.env.local
.jwt-secret
.git/
*.log
